    "profile": {
      "items": [
        {
          "type": "HTML",
          "html": "In the mid 1990s, Robin Singh was viewed as a long-term prospect by many. He had the records to back him up too for he was Delhi's leading wicket taker, striking up a particularly good combination with Atul Wassan. Given this background, his selection in the Indian team for the tour of New Zealand in 1998-99 was not exactly a surprise. But with Srinath, Prasad and Mohanty already in the side,\nit was on the cards that Robin's opportunities would be limited.  But the enthusiastic youngster did well enough in the first-class matches to force his way into the side for the third Test, the  day after his 19th birthday. In a high scoring drawn game, Robin did reasonably well picking up two wickets in the first innings and one in the second. But he became a victim of the selectors' hiring\nand firing policy and that remained the extent of his international career. <BR><b>Partab Ramchand</b>"
        }
      ]
    },
